{"parentUuid":"db5ab176-1b87-43ac-b683-c5088fa5823a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d3b461b0-6c69-4201-b68c-e89ce26c1c77","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user initiated development of **FreeLang Light** - a unified web frontend language combining FreeLang (logic) + CSS (styling) + JavaScript (behavior) in single `.free` component files that compile to separate CSS/JS/HTML outputs. After completing Phase 1-4 of FreeLang Light, the user then proposed and requested creation of a **FreeLang + Next.js Hybrid Stack** where FreeLang handles core logic, state management, and backend (with DB/FFI), while React/Next.js handles UI rendering, SSR, SEO, and routing. The user explicitly requested this hybrid architecture be implemented with \"Bridge\" components connecting the two systems.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Parser/Tokenizer**: Lexical analysis of `.free` files with support for component, props, style, script, markup blocks\n   - **Expression Evaluator**: Safe evaluation of conditions, ternary operators, and arithmetic in templates\n   - **Markup Processor**: Template rendering with conditional (`{if condition ? html : html}`) and loop (`{for item in items ? html}`) support\n   - **Indexer/Search Engine**: Full-text component search with Props/Functions/Styles extraction\n   - **REST API Server**: Port 4002 with /api/search, /api/component endpoints\n   - **Bundler**: Minification, source map generation, manifest creation for production deployment\n   - **State Management**: FreeLang-based store replacing Redux/Vuex with subscribers, watchers, time-travel debugging\n   - **React Bridge**: Custom hooks (useFreeLang, useSelector, useDispatch, useAction) for seamless FreeLang-React integration\n   - **Hybrid Architecture**: FreeLang as state/logic layer, React/Next.js as presentation layer with Bridge middleware\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   **FreeLang Light Project Files:**\n   \n   - **README.md**: Project overview with examples showing usage (compile, search, index, serve commands)\n   \n   - **docs/SPEC.md**: 400+ lines defining language syntax, data types (string, number, boolean, array<T>, object), component structure with Props/Style/Script/Markup blocks, variable substitution\n   \n   - **src/parser.js** (600 lines): \n     - Tokenizer class: Lexical analysis with pattern matching for keywords, strings, numbers, identifiers\n     - Parser class: Recursive descent parser for component definitions\n     - parseFreeLang() function: Entry point returning AST with structure {type, name, props, style, script, markup}\n   \n   - **src/expression-evaluator.js** (300+ lines):\n     - ExpressionEvaluator class for evaluating conditions, ternary operators, arithmetic\n     - Methods: evaluate(), evaluateCondition(), evaluateLoop(), evaluateTernary(), parseDefaultValue()\n     - Support for Props default values parsing (\"string = 'default'\")\n     - Variable extraction from expressions\n   \n   - **src/markup-processor.js** (250+ lines):\n     - MarkupProcessor class for template rendering\n     - processConditions(): {if condition ? true : false} pattern matching\n     - processLoops(): {for item in items ? template} with item_index, item_first, item_last helpers\n     - substituteVariables(): Replace {variable} with actual values\n     - processBindings(): Handle attribute bindings like onclick\n   \n   - **src/indexer.js** (400+ lines):\n     - FreeLangIndexer class that scans .free files and creates searchable index\n     - indexDirectory(), indexFile() methods\n     - extractStyleSelectors(), extractMarkupElements(), generateSearchableText()\n     - calculateRanking() with score based on props count, functions, styles, file size\n     - search() method returning ranked results with match_fields\n     - saveIndex(), loadIndex() for persistence\n     - getStats() returning component count, function count, etc.\n   \n   - **src/search-api.js** (300+ lines):\n     - FreeLangSearchAPI class running on port 4002\n     - Endpoints: /api/health, /api/search?q=, /api/search-three-words?w1=&w2=&w3=, /api/component/{name}, /api/components, /api/docs\n     - CORS enabled for all endpoints\n     - Returns JSON with query, total_results, results array\n     - Integration with indexer for component search\n   \n   - **src/bundler.js** (400+ lines):\n     - Bundler class for CSS/JS/HTML merging\n     - bundleComponents(), bundleComponent() methods\n     - generateCSSBundle(): Merges all CSS with comments and optional minification\n     - generateJSBundle(): Wraps JS functions in IIFE, optional minification\n     - generateHTMLBundle(): Creates full HTML page with script/link tags\n     - minifyCSS(), minifyJS(): Remove comments and unnecessary whitespace\n     - generateSourceMaps(): Create CSS/JS source maps\n     - calculateHash(): SHA256 checksums for integrity\n     - getStats(): Returns component count, file sizes\n   \n   - **src/cli.js** (500+ lines):\n     - FreeLangCLI class with methods for each command\n     - compile <file>: Calls CSSCompiler, JSCompiler, HTMLGenerator, writes output files\n     - search <query>: Calls searchAPI.searchCLI()\n     - index <dir>: Calls indexer.indexDirectory()\n     - bundle <dir>: NEW - Bundler integration\n     - list, stats, serve commands\n     - findFreeLangFiles(), findComponentAssets() helper methods\n   \n   - **src/css-compiler.js** (100 lines):\n     - CSSCompiler class\n     - compile(ast): Transforms style block to CSS\n     - camelToKebab(): Converts backgroundColor to background-color\n     - formatProperties(): Ensures proper CSS property format with semicolons\n   \n   - **src/js-compiler.js** (100 lines):\n     - JSCompiler class\n     - compile(ast): Generates JS from script block\n     - compileFunction(): Wraps functions with proper signatures\n     - getDefaultValue(): Returns default values by type\n   \n   - **src/html-generator.js** (100 lines):\n     - HTMLGenerator class\n     - generate(ast): Creates full HTML page from markup block\n     - transpileMarkup(): Converts {variable} to ${variable}\n     - processBindings(): Handle onclick, onchange attributes\n   \n   - **examples/button.free**: 50-line component with primary/secondary style variants, disabled state, hover effects, onclick handler\n   \n   - **examples/card.free**: 50-line component with header/body/footer sections, hover effects, conditional footer rendering\n   \n   - **examples/list.free**: 50-line component demonstrating conditional rendering (empty message when no items) and loop rendering with first/last item classes\n   \n   - **src/test-phase3.js** (300 lines): 14 tests for ExpressionEvaluator and MarkupProcessor - ALL PASSING\n     - Tests: arithmetic, comparison, string concatenation, ternary operators, array length, default values, variable extraction\n     - Tests: variable substitution, conditional rendering (true/false), loop rendering, index access, first/last flags, nested conditions, bindings\n   \n   - **src/test-bundler.js** (300 lines): 8 tests for Bundler - ALL PASSING\n     - Tests: bundler creation, CSS minification, JS minification, hash calculation, bundle stats, code indentation, actual bundling\n   \n   **FreeLang Hybrid Project Files (NEW):**\n   \n   - **README.md**: Comprehensive documentation of hybrid architecture with ASCII diagram showing Browser (React UI) → Bridge → FreeLang Core → Backend (FreeLang + Node.js)\n     - Explains data flow: browser request → Next.js SSR → Bridge initialization → React components with state → events → FreeLang processing → state change → re-render\n     - Shows example of Counter component with button click incrementing count via FreeLang state\n     - Lists project structure with frontend (pages, components, styles), backend (API, DB), and bridge layers\n     - Outlines 6-phase implementation plan (500-700 lines per phase, 3,500 total)\n   \n   - **bridge/freelang-state.js** (300+ lines):\n     - FreeLangStateManager class - Redux/Vuex replacement built on FreeLang principles\n     - defineState(definition): Initialize state object structure\n     - defineAction(name, handler): Register action handlers\n     - dispatch(actionName, payload): Execute actions with state mutation\n     - getState(path): Retrieve state or nested path (e.g., 'counter.count')\n     - subscribe(listener): Register listeners for state changes, returns unsubscribe function\n     - watch(path, callback): Watch specific state paths with old/new value callbacks\n     - commit(mutationName, payload): Synchronous state changes (alias for dispatch)\n     - getHistory(limit): Retrieve action history\n     - timeTravel(index): Restore to previous state by index\n     - snapshot()/restore(): Save and restore state snapshots\n     - debugLog(): Console logging of current state and history\n     - Global singleton instance: globalStateManager exported\n   \n   - **bridge/hooks.js** (300+ lines): React hooks for FreeLang state integration\n     - useFreeLang(moduleName): Returns state object + dispatch method (e.g., `const {count, increment} = useFreeLang('counter')`)\n     - useSelector(selector): Redux-style selector hook for specific state portions\n     - useDispatch(): Returns dispatch function for manual action calls\n     - useAction(actionName): Creates bound action handler\n     - useActions(actionMap): Batch bind multiple actions at once\n     - useAsyncAction(asyncHandler): Wrapper for async operations with loading/error state\n     - useWatch(path, callback): Side effects on state path changes\n     - useHistory(limit): Returns action history array\n     - useSnapshot(): Save/restore state snapshots with save() and restore() methods\n     - useStore(): Direct access to globalStateManager instance\n     - withStore(Component): HOC for class components\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Regex Pattern Issue in Markup Loop Processing**: Initial regex for {for item in items ? template} was too greedy and didn't capture template content correctly\n     - Fix: Changed regex from `/\\{for\\s+(\\w+)\\s+in\\s+(\\w+)\\s*\\?\\s*(.+?)\\s*\\}/gs` to handle nested braces: `/\\{for\\s+(\\w+)\\s+in\\s+(\\w+)\\s*\\?\\s*((?:[^{}]|\\{[^}]*\\})*?)\\s*\\}/gs`\n     - Confirmed by re-running tests - all 14/14 passed after fix\n   \n   - **first/last Flag Test Format**: Test for `item_first` and `item_last` flags was checking for class attributes with conditional rendering, but the actual HTML generation used data attributes\n     - Fix: Changed test to use data attributes: `data-first=\"{item_first}\"` instead of class binding\n     - Test then passed\n\n   - **GOGS Repository Not Existing**: When trying to push freelang-light to GOGS, got error \"repository not found\"\n     - Context: User provided GOGS URL (https://gogs.dclub.kr/kim/freelang-light.git) - repository was created on server\n     - Fix: Removed and re-added remote with correct URL, successfully pushed\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Parser Design**: Implemented proper tokenizer with state management to handle strings (with escaping), numbers, identifiers, and special characters. Parser uses recursive descent to handle nested blocks.\n   \n   - **Expression Safety**: ExpressionEvaluator uses Function constructor with 'use strict' to safely evaluate expressions while preventing injection attacks. Validates variable names against keywords.\n   \n   - **Search Ranking Algorithm**: Implemented multi-factor ranking considering props count, functions count, styles, markup elements, and file size to provide meaningful search results.\n   \n   - **Loop Variable Context**: Solved template variables in loops by creating itemContext object with original variables plus special variables (item_index, item_first, item_last) for each iteration.\n   \n   - **Minification Safety**: CSS minification preserves important syntax (colons, semicolons, braces) and JS minification preserves function structures while removing comments and extra whitespace.\n   \n   - **State Management Bridge Design**: Created FreeLangStateManager that provides Redux-like dispatch/subscribe pattern but with explicit action registration and immutability through deep copying.\n   \n   - **React Hook Pattern**: Implemented standard React hook patterns (useState, useEffect, useCallback, useContext) for seamless integration with React component lifecycle.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"새 프로젝트 프리랭 라이트 버전 프론트 용 언어 css 자바스크립트 대응 가능한\" (Request for new FreeLang Light project for frontend with CSS and JavaScript support)\n   - \"언어에 통합 버전 어때?\" (Question about integrated language version)\n   - \"고\" (Go - proceed with project)\n   - \"자산부터 파악\" (Understand assets first - referring to GOGS examination)\n   - \"고\" (Go - proceed with Phase 2)\n   - \"고\" (Go - proceed with Phase 3)\n   - \"고\" (Go - proceed with Phase 4)\n   - Long message proposing FreeLang + Next.js Hybrid Architecture with detailed structure, data flow, example code, advantages, and tech stack\n   - \"좋아, 그러면 FreeLang 기반 순수 구현 + 기존 React/Next.js 스택을 함께 쓰는 하이브리드 구조를 설계할 수 있다...\" (Detailed approval and expansion of hybrid architecture proposal with concrete example)\n   - \"그거 만들어줄까?\" (Question: Should I create that?)\n   - \"고\" (Go - proceed with hybrid project)\n   - Request for summary before continuing\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Complete FreeLang Hybrid Phase 1: Bridge Architecture (React Context provider implementation)\n   - Create React Context wrapper for FreeLang state\n   - Implement example components (Counter.tsx, TodoList.tsx) using hooks\n   - Create Next.js page structure (/pages)\n   - Implement Backend API in FreeLang (api.free, handlers.free)\n   - Add FFI/DB integration layer\n   - Create full Next.js SSR example\n   - Performance benchmarking and optimization\n\n8. Current Work:\n   The user has just asked for a comprehensive summary of the conversation. Immediately before this, I had created:\n   \n   **bridge/hooks.js** - The React hooks layer for FreeLang state integration. This file contains 300+ lines defining 11 custom hooks and 1 HOC:\n   ```javascript\n   // Key exports:\n   export function useFreeLang(moduleName) { ... }  // Main hook combining state + dispatch\n   export function useSelector(selector) { ... }    // Redux-style selector\n   export function useDispatch() { ... }            // Dispatch function\n   export function useAction(actionName) { ... }    // Single action binding\n   export function useActions(actionMap) { ... }    // Multiple action binding\n   export function useAsyncAction(asyncHandler) { ... } // Async wrapper\n   export function useWatch(path, callback) { ... } // State path watcher\n   export function useHistory(limit = 10) { ... }   // History hook\n   export function useSnapshot() { ... }            // Snapshot/restore\n   export function useStore() { ... }               // Direct store access\n   export function withStore(Component) { ... }     // HOC for class components\n   ```\n   \n   This completes the Bridge layer foundation (freelang-state.js + hooks.js = 600+ lines total), which is Phase 1 Part 1 of the Hybrid project.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Based on the user's most recent explicit request (\"고\" - proceed with hybrid), the immediate next step would be to continue Phase 1 of the Hybrid project by creating the React Context Provider layer that wraps the FreeLangStateManager and makes it accessible to all React components via Context API. This would enable the hooks to work properly in a Next.js application structure.\n\n   The user's request pattern shows they want to proceed methodically through each phase: they said \"좋아, 그러면 FreeLang 기반 순수 구현... 하이브리드 구조를 설계할 수 있다\" (Excellent, then we can design this hybrid structure) and followed with implementation request \"고\" (Go).