{"parentUuid":"f8acdb11-bc22-4232-ac7b-f3d8211d72e7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"36f2d2f1-3cca-4a58-bc30-fc9b9b5e31d1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Initial: Improve deployment script visibility (Steps 4-6 with port 5020 progress indicators)\n   - Secondary: Integrate FreeLang HTTP Engine into freelang-hybrid project\n   - Tertiary: Implement complete blog functionality in pure FreeLang\n   - Critical Intent: Build standalone FreeLang application WITHOUT Node.js/TypeScript/npm (user explicitly rejected Node.js approach with \"node안쓰는게 목표인데 ??? 자꾸 고집이야\")\n   - Recent: Verify FreeLang capabilities across 8 dimensions (frontend, HTTP, UI, CSS, security, development, self-hosting, Node independence)\n   - Latest: Implement CSS generation system in FreeLang (\"css 정도는 쉽지\" - CSS should be easy)\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - HTTP/1.1 protocol implementation from scratch (TCP sockets → HTTP parsing → REST routing)\n   - Keep-Alive persistent connections (max 100 requests/connection)\n   - CORS header support and automatic Content-Type handling\n   - Blog CRUD operations with state management (DRAFT → PUBLISHED → ARCHIVED)\n   - Type-safe system using record and enum definitions\n   - Layered architecture: TCP Socket Layer → HTTP Parser → Request Handler → Business Logic\n   - Zero external dependencies (FreeLang stdlib only)\n   - FreeLang compiler infrastructure (TypeScript-based, requires npm for build)\n   - CSS generation patterns: dynamic themes, Tailwind-like utilities, CSS-in-JS, responsive design\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **freelang/main.free** (98 lines)\n      - Program entry point, HTTP server initialization\n      - Calls http_server_main(\"0.0.0.0\", 5020, handleEngineRequest)\n      - Loads database on startup, prints system info\n      \n   - **freelang/core/types.free** (136 lines)\n      - Complete type definitions: Counter, Blog, Todo, StateEvent, HealthStatus\n      - Enums: Priority, BlogStatus (DRAFT/PUBLISHED/ARCHIVED), EventType\n      - DatabaseSchema record for JSON structure\n      \n   - **freelang/core/state.free** (231 lines)\n      - Global state variables: counter, todos, blogs, nextBlogId\n      - Counter functions: getCounter(), incrementCounter(), decrementCounter(), resetCounter()\n      - Blog CRUD: createBlog(), getBlogs(status), getBlogById(id), updateBlog(), publishBlog(id), deleteBlog(id)\n      - View/Like tracking: incrementBlogView(id), likeBlog(id)\n      \n   - **freelang/server/http-engine.free** (340 lines)\n      - Main request handler: handleEngineRequest(request) → response\n      - 14 REST API endpoints: Counter (4), Blog (6), Health (1), Static files (2), CORS/404 (1)\n      - Response building with proper status codes (200, 201, 204, 404)\n      - Embedded HTML pages: getIndexHtml() and getBlogHtml() functions\n      - CORS headers automatic application\n      \n   - **freelang/engine/tcp_socket.fl** (312 lines)\n      - Low-level socket management: socket(), bind(), listen(), accept(), read(), write(), close()\n      - SO_REUSEADDR configuration, timeout setting\n      - Helper functions for network byte order conversion\n      \n   - **freelang/engine/http_parser.fl** (364 lines)\n      - HTTP/1.1 request parsing from raw bytes\n      - Request line parsing (method, path, version)\n      - Headers parsing with validation\n      - Body extraction based on Content-Length\n      - Validation for HTTP methods and versions\n      \n   - **freelang/engine/http_handler.fl** (322 lines)\n      - HTTP response generation\n      - Serialization of structured responses to bytes\n      - Content-Type and Content-Length calculation\n      \n   - **freelang/engine/server.fl** (311 lines)\n      - Main server loop with accept() loop\n      - Keep-Alive support (persistent connections)\n      - Multi-request handling per connection\n      \n   - **data/db.json** (71 lines)\n      - 3 sample blogs: \"FreeLang HTTP Server 완성\" (PUBLISHED), \"메모리 관리 시스템\" (PUBLISHED), \"Type Safety와 패턴 매칭\" (DRAFT)\n      - Counter initial state (count: 0)\n      - Todo and Events structures\n      \n   - **blog-posts/001-freelang-http-server.md** (215 lines)\n      - First technical blog post: \"Node.js 없이 완벽한 HTTP 서버를 만들다\"\n      - Sections: Introduction, Implementation scale, Architecture, Code examples, Performance comparison, Motivation\n      \n   - **freelang/ARCHITECTURE.md** (80 lines)\n      - Complete system architecture documentation\n      - Data flow diagram (Client → TCP → HTTP Parser → Request Handler → State → Response → TCP → Client)\n      - Type definitions and REST endpoint listing\n      \n   - **freelang/README.md** (150 lines)\n      - Quick start guide with build and run commands\n      - API testing examples (curl commands for all endpoints)\n      - Web UI documentation (homepage and blog page)\n      \n   - **PROJECT_STATUS.md** (199 lines)\n      - Detailed completion status for all components\n      - Statistics: 2,150 lines code, 14 endpoints, 7 type definitions\n      - 3-step roadmap for next phases\n      \n   - **test-api.sh** (Auto-generated)\n      - Automated API testing script for all 14 endpoints\n      - Tests Counter, Blog, Health Check, Static files, 404\n      - Validates HTTP status codes and response format\n      \n   - **simulate-api.sh** (Auto-generated)\n      - API simulation script showing blog statistics\n      - Lists 3 sample blogs with metadata\n      - Provides curl commands for testing\n      \n   - **setup-freelang.sh** (Auto-generated)\n      - 5-step automatic setup: compiler check, file validation, compilation, data verification, server startup\n      - Includes FreeLang installation instructions\n      \n   - **RUN_NOW.md** (400 lines)\n      - Detailed execution guide with