ies (gray, blue, red, green, yellow, purple) each with 10 shades (50-900)\n      - Breakpoints: xs(320px), sm(640px), md(768px), lg(1024px), xl(1280px)\n      - Font sizes: xs(12px) to 5xl(48px)\n      - Border radius: 9 options from none(0) to full(9999px)\n      - Shadows: 8 shadow definitions from sm to 2xl\n\n   **freelang/core/tailwind-utils.free** (300+ lines)\n      - Critical: Generates all basic utility CSS classes used by HTML elements\n      - Functions: generateDisplayClasses(), generateSpacingClasses(), generateColorClasses(), generateTypographyClasses(), generateBorderClasses(), generateEffectClasses(), generateSizeClasses(), generateAllUtilityClasses()\n      - Display utilities: flex, grid, block, hidden, inline variants\n      - Flexbox: flex-row, flex-col, justify-center, items-center, gap utilities\n      - Spacing: padding (p-0 to p-12), margin (m-0 to m-8), directional variants (px-, py-, mt-, mb-, mx-, my-)\n      - Colors: 60+ background and text color combinations\n      - Typography: font-size (8 variants), font-weight (9 variants), text-align, line-height, letter-spacing\n      - Borders: border styles, colors, radius (7 variants), divide utilities\n      - Effects: shadows (8 variants), opacity (5 levels), transform scale, transitions\n      - Size utilities: width (auto, percentages, viewport units), height, max-width breakpoints\n\n   **freelang/core/css-generator.free** (450 lines - Phase 6)\n      - Dynamic CSS variable generation\n      - 11 CSS generation functions\n      - Theme system support (light, dark, purple)\n      - Responsive design with 5 breakpoints\n      - 60+ utility classes\n\n   **freelang/core/ui-generator.free** (1,200 lines - Phase 7)\n      - Search page with filtering and pagination\n      - Admin dashboard with statistics and management table\n      - User profile page with activity stats and tech stack\n      - Improved homepage with navigation, hero section, feature cards\n      - Theme switcher (Light/Dark)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - File not read before edit: Fixed by reading files first with Read tool before using Edit\n   - Module path issues in FreeLang imports: Resolved by using correct relative paths with \"../core/module-name\"\n   - String replacement not found in file: Occurred because file content had subtle formatting differences - fixed by reading file first to get exact formatting\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Implemented complete HTTP server (Phase 1-5) before this session with 14 API endpoints\n   - Resolved user's critical feedback about Node.js usage - immediately stopped Node.js approach and pivoted to pure FreeLang\n   - Designed 7-phase Tailwind implementation with clear separation: MVP (8-10), Automation (11-12), Advanced (13-14)\n   - Created scalable architecture where FreeLang defines all scales and generates CSS, while JavaScript handles runtime class manipulation\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"그래서 어디서 보는데??\" (So where do you see it?)\n   - \"서버실행\" (Run server)\n   - \"프리랭 http 서버 활용\" (Utilize FreeLang HTTP server)\n   - \"a\" (Selected Option A)\n   - \"계속 진행 블로그 완성 해봐\" (Continue and complete blog)\n   - \"node안쓰는게 목표인데 ??? 자꾸 고집이야\" (Goal is no Node.js, but you keep insisting - CRITICAL FEEDBACK)\n   - \"블로그 시작\" (Blog start)\n   - \"실행\" (Execute/Run)\n   - \"컴파일은 https://gogs.dclub.kr/kim/freelang-v2.git 여기 있음\" (Compiler is at GOGS repo)\n   - \"당연히 됩니다! (권장하진 않지만): 이건 다른 생각임 css 만들면 ??\" (Of course! Different thinking - what about CSS generation?)\n   - \"프리랭도 만들기 어려웠음 css 정도는 쉽지\" (FreeLang was hard to make, CSS should be easy)\n   - \"좋아 진행\" (Good, proceed)\n   - \"좋다. 이번엔 FreeLang + JS 환경에서 Tailwind를 \"직접 구현\"하는 로드맵을 단계별로 설계해준다.\" (Good. This time design a step-by-step roadmap for directly implementing Tailwind in FreeLang + JS environment)\n   - \"좋아 시작[Request interrupted by user]완전 구현 (Phase 8-14): 완성도 높음\" (Good start [interrupted] Complete implementation Phase 8-14: High completion)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Phase 10: Responsive system implementation (freelang/core/tailwind-responsive.free - 400 lines)\n   - Phase 11: State utilities (hover, active, focus, disabled) - (freelang/core/tailwind-states.free - 200 lines)\n   - Phase 12: FreeLang CSS generation engine that converts config scales to CSS - (freelang/core/tailwind-generator.free - 600 lines)\n   - Phase 13: Class parser to extract used classes from HTML - (freelang/core/tailwind-parser.free - 400 lines)\n   - Phase 14: JS runtime for dynamic class manipulation - (frontend/tailwind-runtime.js - 300 lines)\n   - Phase 15: Optimizer and build automation (build-tailwind.sh - 50 lines)\n   - Update HTTP engine to serve dynamic tailwind.css endpoint\n   - Update project documentation with MiniTailwind architecture\n   - Integration with existing HTTP server and UI pages\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was implementing Phase 8 and Phase 9 of the MiniTailwind system:\n   \n   **Phase 8 - Configuration (COMPLETED)**\n   - File: freelang/core/tailwind-config.free\n   - Created getTailwindConfig() function that returns object with:\n     - spacing: 18 scale values (0, 4px, 8px, 12px... 256px)\n     - colors: 6 color families × 10 shades each = 60 colors\n     - breakpoints: xs, sm, md, lg, xl\n     - fontSize: xs(12px) through 5xl(48px)\n     - borderRadius: none through full(9999px)\n     - shadows: sm through 2xl with specific shadow definitions\n   \n   **Phase 9 - Utility Classes (COMPLETED)**\n   - File: freelang/core/tailwind-utils.free\n   - Implemented 8 generation functions that output CSS:\n     - Display classes: flex, grid, block, hidden, inline variants\n     - Spacing: Comprehensive padding/margin utilities (p-0 to p-12, m-0 to m-8)\n     - Colors: 60+ background and text color combinations\n     - Typography: Font sizes, weights, text alignment, line heights\n     - Borders: Styles, colors, radius variants\n     - Effects: Shadows, opacity, scale transforms, transitions\n     - Size utilities: Width, height, max-width with various units\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue immediately with **Phase 10: Responsive System Implementation** as explicitly requested in the user's message \"좋아 시작...완전 구현 (Phase 8-14)\". The next file to create is `freelang/core/tailwind-responsive.free` (400 lines) which will implement @media query generation for the 5 breakpoints (xs, sm, md, lg, xl) and generate responsive utility variants like `md-flex`, `lg-p-4`, `xl-grid-cols-3`, etc. This phase is essential to enable responsive design before moving to state utilities in Phase 11.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /data/data/com.termux/files/home/.claude/projects/-data-data-com-termux-files-home/11d51b2b-7fd0-400a-a001-be95ead172d4.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"b88d0ee2-820f-4c18-b191-d84d29bd4636","timestamp":"2026-03-12T14:31:16.389Z","userType":"external","cwd":"/data/data/com.termux/files/home/freelang-hybrid","sessionId":"11d51b2b-7fd0-400a-a001-be95ead172d4","version":"2.1.74","gitBranch":"master","slug":"purrfect-hatching-lecun"}
