{"parentUuid":"3293ec36-c00a-4d32-b3ad-4fb7d953361f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4774e8de-4c84-4c08-ab07-3ba8c63e3966","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user requested a complete implementation of MiniTailwind (a Tailwind CSS system built in FreeLang + JavaScript) with Phases 8-15, then deployment, and finally execution with visibility. The user specifically selected \"완전 구현 (Phase 8-14): 완성도 높음\" indicating they wanted a fully complete, production-ready implementation.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Tailwind CSS Utility System (atomic CSS approach)\n   - JIT (Just-In-Time) CSS compilation - only generate CSS for used classes\n   - 5 Responsive Breakpoints (xs: 320px, sm: 640px, md: 768px, lg: 1024px, xl: 1280px)\n   - State utilities (hover, active, focus, disabled, dark mode)\n   - FreeLang as backend/configuration language\n   - JavaScript runtime for dynamic class manipulation and theme switching\n   - HTTP server integration for serving CSS and JavaScript\n   - localStorage for persistence of user theme choices\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   **Phase 8-15 Implementation Files Created:**\n   \n   - **freelang/core/tailwind-config.free** (225 lines)\n     - Defines all Tailwind configuration as single source of truth\n     - Color palette: 6 colors × 10 shades (60 total colors)\n     - Spacing scale: 18 values from 0 to 256px in 4px increments\n     - 5 breakpoints, font sizes, border radius, shadows\n     - Key function: getTailwindConfig() returns object with all scales\n   \n   - **freelang/core/tailwind-utils.free** (300 lines)\n     - Generates basic utility CSS classes used in HTML\n     - Functions: generateDisplayClasses(), generateSpacingClasses(), generateColorClasses(), generateTypographyClasses(), generateBorderClasses(), generateEffectClasses(), generateSizeClasses()\n     - Output: CSS for flex, grid, padding, margin, colors, typography, borders, shadows\n   \n   - **freelang/core/tailwind-responsive.free** (400 lines)\n     - Generates responsive utility classes for 5 breakpoints\n     - Functions: generateResponsiveDisplayClasses(), generateResponsivePaddingClasses(), generateResponsiveMarginClasses(), generateResponsiveFontSizeClasses(), generateResponsiveSizeClasses(), generateResponsiveFlexClasses(), generateResponsiveGridClasses(), generateResponsiveTextClasses(), generateResponsiveBorderClasses()\n     - Output: Classes like sm-flex, md-p-4, lg-grid-cols-3, xl-text-xl\n   \n   - **freelang/core/tailwind-states.free** (280 lines)\n     - Generates state-based utility classes for pseudo-classes\n     - Functions: generateHoverClasses(), generateActiveClasses(), generateFocusClasses(), generateDisabledClasses(), generateGroupStateClasses(), generateChildStateClasses(), generateDarkModeClasses(), generateTransitionClasses()\n     - Output: hover-bg-blue-500, focus-ring, active-scale-95, dark-bg-gray-900\n   \n   - **freelang/core/tailwind-generator.free** (350 lines)\n     - CSS generation engine converting all config scales to CSS\n     - Functions: generateCSSVariables(), generateResetCSS(), generateUtilityCSS(), generateResponsiveCSS(), generateStateCSS(), generateComponentStyles(), generateCompleteTailwindCSS(), generateLightThemeCSS(), generateDarkThemeCSS(), calculateCSSSize(), generateCSSStatistics()\n     - Generates CSS Variables, Reset CSS, Component base styles, Light/Dark themes\n   \n   - **freelang/core/tailwind-parser.free** (350 lines)\n     - Class parser and JIT compiler extracting used classes from HTML\n     - Functions: extractClassesFromHTML(), classifyClass(), isValidTailwindClass(), generateCSSRule(), generateJITCSS(), analyzeClassUsage()\n     - JIT compilation: only generate CSS for classes actually used in HTML\n   \n   - **frontend/tailwind-runtime.js** (480 lines)\n     - JavaScript runtime for dynamic class manipulation and theme switching\n     - Class: TailwindRuntime with methods:\n       - loadTailwindCSS(): dynamically load CSS based on theme\n       - switchTheme(theme): toggle between light/dark, save to localStorage\n       - getCurrentBreakpoint(): detect current responsive breakpoint\n       - setupResponsiveListener(): monitor window resize and update breakpoint\n       - addClass(), removeClass(), toggleClass(), applyClass(): dynamic class manipulation\n       - observeDOM(): MutationObserver to track dynamically added elements\n       - enableDebugMode(): expose window.tailwind for console access\n     - Convenience functions: tailwindSetTheme(), tailwindToggleDarkMode(), tailwindAddClass(), tailwindRemoveClass(), tailwindToggleClass()\n   \n   - **build-tailwind.sh** (280 lines)\n     - Bash build script for automation\n     - Steps: Check required files, verify FreeLang compiler, generate CSS files, optimize and copy, provide build summary\n     - Output: styles.css (8KB), styles-dark.css (4KB)\n   \n   **Deployment Integration:**\n   \n   - **freelang/server/http-engine.free** (modified)\n     - Added GET /styles.css endpoint serving light theme CSS\n     - Added GET /styles-dark.css endpoint serving dark theme CSS\n     - Added GET /tailwind-runtime.js endpoint serving JavaScript runtime (new endpoint)\n     - Added getTailwindRuntime() function (~450 lines) containing full JavaScript runtime code\n     - Updated getIndexHtml() to include <script src=\"/tailwind-runtime.js\" defer></script>\n     - Updated getBlogHtml() to include <script src=\"/tailwind-runtime.js\" defer></script>\n     - Changes: 488 insertions for deployment support\n   \n   - **public/css/styles.css** (8KB)\n     - Light theme CSS generated by build-tailwind.sh\n     - Contains: CSS variables, reset styles, all utility classes, responsive variants, state classes\n   \n   - **public/css/styles-dark.css** (4KB)\n     - Dar