{"parentUuid":"2976b6f5-6119-4623-8f1a-2a49eb796863","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"159099eb-f8b4-4430-893c-b8071c6bc2d4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent:**\n   The user requested creation of a complete FreeLang CSS system + 3-server web infrastructure with zero external dependencies (npm, pip). The critical evolution occurred when user pointed out inconsistency: if FreeLang HTTP servers were being created, they should be used instead of falling back to external tools. This led to the final explicit request: \"3개 웹서버 - 모두 즉시 실행가능 정공법으로 역설계 정식 프리랭 모듈 로 가능하게 재설계\" (redesign 3 web servers as formal FreeLang modules, all immediately executable, proper reverse-engineering approach). The intent evolved from generic CSS framework to pure FreeLang ecosystem with zero dependencies.\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts:**\n   - MiniTailwind CSS: 500+ utility classes, 5 responsive breakpoints (xs/sm/md/lg/xl), Light/Dark themes, CSS variables\n   - FreeLang CSS Module System: Type-safe CSS generation with components (Button, Card, Input, Badge)\n   - Zero-Dependency Architecture: No npm, pip, Node.js, or Python required for deployment\n   - FreeLang Standard Library: std/net (sockets), std/http (HTTP protocol), std/fs (file I/O), std/json (JSON handling)\n   - Weighted Round-Robin Load Balancing: Proxy server with upstream selection and health checks\n   - HTTP Server Protocol: Request parsing, static file serving, MIME type detection\n   - REST API: 5 endpoints (/api/posts, /api/posts/:id, /api/theme, /api/health, POST /api/posts)\n   - Build Automation: FreeLang-based build system replacing npm scripts\n   - Compilation Strategy: freec compiler for native binaries or freelang runtime for direct execution\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections:**\n\n   **Core FreeLang Web Servers (Final Redesign):**\n   \n   - **freelang/servers/http-main.free (227 lines)**\n     - Purpose: Formal HTTP static file server with full main() entry point, independently compilable and executable\n     - Key Functions: main(), createHTTPServer(), startServer(), parseHTTPRequest(), serveStaticFile(), getMimeType(), buildHTTPResponse(), runServerLoop()\n     - Uses: std/net, std/fs, std/http\n     - Compiles: `freec http-main.free -o http-server`\n     - Executes: `./http-server` or `freelang http-main.free`\n     - Serves: blog.html, CSS files, JavaScript runtime from current directory\n     - Code Structure:\n       ```freelang\n       type HTTPServer = {\n         host: string,\n         port: i32,\n         socket: i32,\n         running: bool,\n         requestCount: i32\n       }\n       \n       func main() -> void {\n         let server = createHTTPServer(\"127.0.0.1\", 8000)\n         if startServer(server) {\n           runServerLoop(server)\n         }\n       }\n       ```\n\n   - **freelang/servers/api-main.free (244 lines)**\n     - Purpose: Formal REST API server with 5 endpoints, independently compilable and executable\n     - Key Functions: main(), createAPIServer(), createSampleBlogs(), handleAPIRequest(), blogToJSON(), blogsToJSON(), getBlogById(), runAPILoop()\n     - Uses: std/net, std/json, std/http\n     - Compiles: `freec api-main.free -o api-server`\n     - Executes: `./api-server` or `freelang api-main.free`\n     - Endpoints:\n       - GET /api/posts - returns blog list as JSON\n       - GET /api/posts/:id - returns specific blog\n       - GET /api/theme?dark=true - returns theme configuration\n       - GET /api/health - returns server status\n       - POST /api/posts - creates new blog (auth required)\n     - Code Structure:\n       ```freelang\n       type Blog = {\n         id: i32,\n         title: string,\n         excerpt: string,\n         date: string,\n         author: string,\n         category: string,\n         views: i32\n       }\n       \n       func main() -> void {\n         let server = createAPIServer(\"127.0.0.1\", 8001)\n         if startAPIServer(server) {\n           runAPILoop(server)\n         }\n       }\n       ```\n\n   - **freelang/servers/proxy-main.free (283 lines)**\n     - Purpose: Formal load balancer/proxy with Weighted Round-Robin, auto health checks, independently compilable\n     - Key Functions: main(), createProxyServer(), startProxyServer(), selectUpstream(), forwardRequest(), runHealthChecks(), runProxyLoop(), printProxyStats()\n     - Uses: std/net, std/http\n     - Compiles: `freec proxy-main.free -o proxy-server`\n     - Executes: `./proxy-server` or `freelang proxy-main.free`\n     - Load Balancing: Weighted Round-Robin with upstream1 (port 8000, weight 5) and upstream2 (port 8001, weight 3)\n     - Health Checks: 10-second intervals\n     - Code Structure:\n       ```freelang\n       type Upstream = {\n         id: string,\n         host: string,\n         port: i32,\n         weight: i32,\n         healthy: bool,\n         requestCount: i32\n       }\n       \n       func main() -> void {\n         let server = createProxyServer(\"127.0.0.1\", 9000)\n         if startProxyServer(server) {\n           runProxyLoop(server)\n         }\n       }\n       ```\n\n   **Build & Execution Infrastructure:**\n   \n   - **build-servers.sh**\n     - Purpose: Automatically detects FreeLang compiler and compiles all 3 server modules\n     - Detects: freec or freelang\n     - Compiles: http-main.free → http-server, api-main.free → api-server, proxy-main.free → proxy-server\n     - Output: .build/servers/ directory with compiled binaries\n\n   - **run-freelang-servers.sh**\n     - Purpose: Automatically builds (if needed) and runs all 3 servers with 4 execution methods\n     - Auto-detects FreeLang runtime\n     - Checks port availability (8000, 8001, 9000)\n     - Starts 3 servers in background with PIDs\n     - Handles Ctrl+C cleanup\n     - Supports 4 execution methods:\n       1. Automatic build+run: `bash run-freelang-servers.sh`\n       2. Manual compile: `bash build-servers.sh` then run binaries\n       3. Runtime execution: `freelang freelang/servers/http-main.free`\n       4. Compiler execution: `freec freelang/servers/http-main.free && ./http-main`\n\n   **Supporting FreeLang Modules (Earlier):**\n   \n   - **freelang/core/css-module.free (409 lines)**\n     - Type-safe CSS generation with color definitions (60), spacing (12), typography\n     - Functions: defineColors(), defineSpacing(), defineTypography(), defineBreakpoints()\n     - Generates CSS variables and utility classes\n\n   - **freelang/core/css-components.free (363 lines)**\n     - UI components: Button, Card, Input, Badge with variants\n     - Each component has base styles, hover/focus states, and color variants\n     - Example Button component with primary/secondary/danger/success variants\n\n   - **freelang/core/build-system.free (661 lines)**\n     - Build automation: CSS building, JavaScript building, testing, linting, packaging\n     - Types: BuildConfig, BuildResult, TestCase, TestResult, LintResult, Package\n     - Functions: buildCSS(), buildJavaScript(), runTests(), lintFile(), createPackage()\n     - Returns detailed build results with success status, timing, sizes, errors, warnings\n\n   **Web Assets:**\n   \n   - **public/css/styles.css (6.1 KB)**\n     - 500+ utility classes generated from MiniTailwind\n     - CSS variables for colors, spacing, typography\n     - Responsive breakpoints (xs/sm/md/lg/xl)\n     - All utilities: display, spacing, colors, typography, border, shadow, sizing\n\n   - **public/css/styles-dark.css (170 B)**\n     - Dark theme CSS variable overrides\n     - Minimal override file using CSS variables\n\n   - **frontend/tailwind-runtime.js (11 KB)**\n     - Pure JavaScript (no dependencies)\n     - TailwindRuntime class with methods: loadTailwindCSS(), switchTheme(), addClass/removeClass/toggleClass()\n     - localStorage