{"parentUuid":"dad9be1e-b02c-4785-ab80-b8e88d8b9bda","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6c999395-2b62-4699-900a-82f99e540389","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user undertook a comprehensive FreeLang web server project with the explicit goal of creating a complete, production-ready system with zero external dependencies. The primary intent evolved through several critical pivots:\n   \n   - Initial: Run existing web servers\n   - Critical pivot: Realize Python/Bash servers contradicted the \"0 dependencies\" goal, demand complete redesign as formal FreeLang modules\n   - Final: Implement 5 phases (Networking, Database, JWT Auth, HTTPS/TLS, Microservices) with detailed task-based checklists to completion\n   \n   Key explicit requests in order:\n   1. \"3개 웹서버 - 모두 즉시 실행가능 정공법으로 역설계 정식 프리랭 모듈 로 가능하게 재설계\" - Redesign servers as formal FreeLang modules\n   2. Multiple \"gogs 저장\" requests - Save to GOGS repository\n   3. \"kpm 등록?\" - Register on kpm package manager\n   4. \"사용자 커뮤니케이션 ?? 느낀점 아시운점 보안점\" - Provide comprehensive project analysis\n   5. Security features: \"파일 경로 traversal 방지, URL 파라미터 검증, API 인증 추가, HTTPS/TLS 지원 추가 구성\"\n   6. \"전부\" - Implement all 5 production phases\n   7. \"완성까지 가자 스케줄대로 체크리스트 만들고 체크하면서 진행\" - Go to completion with schedule-based checklists\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - FreeLang: A new programming language being developed, used exclusively for this project\n   - Zero-dependency architecture: No npm, pip, Node.js, or Python in production deployment\n   - Formal modules: FreeLang code files with main() entry points that can be compiled to binaries\n   - std/net: FreeLang standard library for network operations (TCP sockets)\n   - std/http: FreeLang standard library for HTTP protocol\n   - std/fs: FreeLang standard library for file I/O\n   - std/json: FreeLang standard library for JSON handling\n   - Weighted Round-Robin: Load balancing algorithm implemented in proxy server\n   - MiniTailwind CSS: 500+ utility CSS classes framework\n   - JWT (JSON Web Tokens): Token-based authentication with HMAC-SHA256\n   - HTTPS/TLS: Encrypted communication protocol\n   - Microservices architecture: Service registry, discovery, health checks\n   - SQLite/File-based database: Data persistence layer\n   - GOGS: Git server for repository management\n   - kpm: FreeLang package manager\n   - Build automation: Bash scripts for compilation and execution\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   Core Web Server Modules:\n   - freelang/servers/http-main.free (260+ lines)\n     * Purpose: HTTP static file server on port 8000\n     * Key functions: parseHTTPRequest(), serveStaticFile(), getMimeType(), buildHTTPResponse()\n     * Recent additions: isPathSafe() validation function to prevent path traversal attacks\n     * Code snippet:\n       ```freelang\n       func isPathSafe(path: string) -> bool {\n         if path.startsWith(\"/\") { return false }\n         if path.contains(\"..\") { return false }\n         if path.contains(\"\\0\") { return false }\n         if path.contains(\"/.\") { return false }\n         if path.startsWith(\".\") { return false }\n         return isAllowedExtension(path)\n       }\n       ```\n\n   - freelang/servers/api-main.free (310+ lines)\n     * Purpose: REST API server on port 8001 with 5 endpoints\n     * Key functions: handleAPIRequest(), blogToJSON(), getBlogById()\n     * Recent additions: isValidBlogId(), isValidQueryParam() for parameter validation\n     * Endpoints: GET /api/posts, GET /api/posts/:id, GET /api/theme, GET /api/health, POST /api/posts\n     * Code snippet for validation:\n       ```freelang\n       func isValidBlogId(idStr: string) -> bool {\n         if idStr.isEmpty() || idStr.length() > 10 { return false }\n         for i in 0..idStr.length() {\n           if !isDigitChar(idStr[i]) { return false }\n         }\n         return true\n       }\n       ```\n\n   - freelang/servers/proxy-main.free (270+ lines)\n     * Purpose: Load balancer on port 9000 with Weighted Round-Robin\n     * Key functions: selectUpstream(), forwardRequest(), runHealthChecks()\n     * Features: 2 upstream servers (8000 weight 5, 8001 weight 3)\n\n   Security Module:\n   - freelang/core/security-utils.free (490 lines)\n     * 7 sections: Path traversal prevention, URL parameter validation, API authentication, Rate limiting, Security headers, HTTPS/TLS config, Utilities\n     * Key types: validateFilePath(), validateURLParameter(), generateToken(), createRateLimiter(), getSecurityHeaders()\n     * Provides reusable security functions for all servers\n\n   Production System Module:\n   - freelang/core/production-system.free (450 lines)\n     * Phase 2: DatabaseConnection, BlogRecord, CRUD functions\n     * Phase 3: JWTConfig, JWTToken, JWT generation/verification\n     * Phase 4: TLSServerConfig, TLSConnection, encryption\n     * Phase 5: ServiceRegistry, service discovery\n     * Code patterns for all phases with proper types and function signatures\n\n   Networking Module:\n   - freelang/core/networking.free (450 lines)\n     * Phase 1 implementation: ServerSocket, ClientConnection types\n     * TCP socket management: bindSocket(), acceptConnection(), readFromSocket(), writeToSocket()\n     * HTTP handling: parseHTTPRequest(), buildHTTPResponse()\n     * ConnectionPool for multi-client support\n     * Error handling and network statistics\n\n   Build Infrastructure:\n   - build-servers.sh: Auto-detects FreeLang compiler (freec/freelang), compiles all 3 servers to .build/servers/\n   - run-freelang-servers.sh: Builds if needed, checks port availability (8000, 8001, 9000), starts 3 servers in background with cleanup\n\n   Package Manifests:\n   - kpm.yaml (freelang-v2): 6 modules (3 servers + 3 libraries), 134 lines\n   - kpm.yaml (freela