ase 5 enhancements.\n\n   **Work State**: All Phase 1-5 implementation complete, tested, evaluated, and committed to GOGS. System is production-ready at 95/100 completeness. Awaiting explicit user direction on whether to implement the suggested improvements or pursue other tasks.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   **Clarification Needed**: The user quoted the Phase 2 and Phase 5 improvement recommendations but has not explicitly requested implementation. The most appropriate next step would be to await explicit user confirmation on:\n   1. Whether they want Phase 2 Database upgraded to SQLite with transaction/concurrency support\n   2. Whether they want Phase 5 Microservices enhanced with circuit breaker pattern and weighted load balancing\n   3. Whether they want both improvements implemented concurrently or sequentially\n   \n   If the user confirms, the implementation would follow this order:\n   - Phase 2: Create new `freelang/core/database-sqlite.js` with SQLite3 module integration, transaction support, and optimistic/pessimistic locking\n   - Phase 5: Create `freelang/core/circuit-breaker.js` with failure threshold detection, half-open states, and weighted service routing\n   - Integration: Update http-server-phase2.js and http-server-phase3.js to use SQLite backend\n   - Testing: Create new integration tests for transaction rollback, concurrent writes, circuit breaker state transitions\n   - GOGS Commit: \"✨ Phase 2: SQLite database with transactions + Phase 5: Circuit breaker pattern\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /data/data/com.termux/files/home/.claude/projects/-data-data-com-termux-files-home/11d51b2b-7fd0-400a-a001-be95ead172d4.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll